Z||000000||Hank is Here||11-25-2000||12:15 AM||||Okay,I am in the process of pulling a 2.5 out of an 84 se with ac.  I an not sure what motor is going in place in the future but I can't figure two things out, i just don't want to destroy them.<BR>A) how do you disconnect the throttle cable?<BR>B) I can't seem to get the coolant hose gonig to the water pump off because the ac pump is in the way.  <P>Any ideas????<BR>Thanks ahead of time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Brian84SE||11-26-2000||07:47 AM||||You have to remove the clip where it goes on the linkage. Lift the tang and slide the whole clip.  If it's anything like mine, it will fall onto the ground, never to be found again. There are 2 tangs that hold the assy. in place. You must squeeze them and push the assy. back out(good luck).<P>Remove the a/c compressor and the hose will be easy to get off.||||reg||1
